Acceptable academic resources vary across fields and departments.Ê It is the studentÕs responsibility to discuss tools and resources with course instructors, advisors, and departments before use unless explicitly authorized in advance and to appropriately cite all resources and tools used in all academic work.
PlagiarismÊis the act of taking the words, ideas, data, illustrations, or statements of another person, program, or source, and presenting them as one's own.ÊThis includes using the assistance of artificial intelligence (A.I.) text generators to perform central requirements of an assignment (i.e. reading, synthesizing, interpreting, writing, coding, programming, etc.) without both the explicit permission of the instructor and complete attribution and citation of A.I. assisted components.
